#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Definition of purifications {#definition-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Kahulugan ng mga purification {#definition-of-purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let us begin with a precise mathematical definition for purifications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula tayo sa isang tiyak na mathematical na kahulugan ng mga "
"purification.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system in a state represented by a density matrix $\\rho,$ and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a quantum state vector of a pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that leaves $\\rho$ when $\\mathsf{Y}$ is traced out:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is then said to be a *purification* of $\\rho.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Kahulugan\">\n"
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ ay isang sistema na nasa estado na kinakatawan ng density matrix na $\\rho,$ at ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay isang quantum state vector ng pares na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ na nagbubunga ng $\\rho$ kapag na-trace out ang $\\mathsf{Y}$:\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
"Ang state vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay tinatawag na *purification* ng $\\rho.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,$ expressed as a "
"density matrix rather than a quantum state vector, is also commonly referred"
" to as a purification of $\\rho$ when the equation in the definition is "
"true, but we'll generally use the term to refer to a quantum state vector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pure state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert,$ na isinulat "
"bilang density matrix sa halip na quantum state vector, ay madalas ding "
"tinatawag na purification ng $\\rho$ kapag totoo ang equation sa kahulugan, "
"ngunit sa pangkalahatan ay gagamitin natin ang terminong ito para tumukoy sa"
" isang quantum state vector.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The term *purification* is also used more generally when the ordering of the systems is reversed, when the names of the systems and states are different (of course), and when there are more than two systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ is a quantum state vector representing a pure state of a compound system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ and the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Ginagamit din ang terminong *purification* sa mas malawak na konteksto — kapag binaliktad ang pagkakasunud-sunod ng mga sistema, kapag iba ang mga pangalan ng mga sistema at estado (syempre), at kapag may higit sa dalawang sistema.\n"
"Halimbawa, kung ang $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ ay isang quantum state vector na kumakatawan sa isang pure state ng compound system na $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ at totoo ang equation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is true for a density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the system "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C}),$ then $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is still referred to"
" as a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa isang density matrix na $\\rho$ na kumakatawan sa estado ng sistema "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{C}),$ kung gayon ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay "
"tinatawag pa rin na purification ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the purposes of this lesson, however, we'll focus on the specific form described in the definition.\n"
"Properties and facts concerning purifications, according to this definition, can typically be generalized to more than two systems by re-ordering and partitioning the systems into two compound systems, one playing the role of $\\mathsf{X}$ and the other playing the role of $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa layunin ng araling ito, gagawin nating focus ang partikular na anyo na inilarawan sa kahulugan.\n"
"Ang mga katangian at katotohanan tungkol sa mga purification, ayon sa kahulugang ito, ay karaniwang maaaring gawing pangkalahatan para sa higit sa dalawang sistema sa pamamagitan ng muling pag-aayos at pag-partition ng mga sistema sa dalawang compound system — isa ang gumaganap ng papel ng $\\mathsf{X}$ at isa ang gumaganap ng papel ng $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Existence of purifications {#existence-of-purifications}"
msgstr "Pag-iral ng mga purification {#existence-of-purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are any two systems and $\\rho$ is a given state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"We will prove that there exists a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that *purifies* $\\rho$ — which is another way of saying that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is a purification of $\\rho$ — provided that the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is large enough.\n"
"In particular, if $\\mathsf{Y}$ has at least as many classical states as $\\mathsf{X},$ then a purification of this form necessarily exists for every state $\\rho.$\n"
"Fewer classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are required for some states $\\rho;$\n"
"in general, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ are necessary and sufficient for the existence of a quantum state vector of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that purifies $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay anumang dalawang sistema at ang $\\rho$ ay isang ibinigay na estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Patutunayan natin na mayroon talagang quantum state vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ na *nagpu-purify* ng $\\rho$ — ibig sabihin, ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay purification ng $\\rho$ — basta't malaki ang sapat na sistema $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Sa partikular, kung ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay may kasing-dami o higit pang classical states kaysa sa $\\mathsf{X},$ kung gayon ang purification ng ganitong anyo ay tiyak na mayroon para sa bawat estado na $\\rho.$\n"
"Mas kaunting classical states ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ ang kailangan para sa ilang estado na $\\rho;$\n"
"sa pangkalahatan, $\\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ na classical states ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ ang kinakailangan at sapat para sa pag-iral ng isang quantum state vector ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ na nagpu-purify ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first any expression of $\\rho$ as a convex combination of $n$ pure"
" states, for any positive integer $n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang muna ang anumang pagpapahayag ng $\\rho$ bilang convex "
"combination ng $n$ pure states, para sa anumang positibong integer na $n.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this expression, $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ is a probability vector and "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are quantum state "
"vectors of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagpapahayag na ito, ang $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ ay isang probability "
"vector at ang $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ ay "
"mga quantum state vector ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to obtain such an expression is through the spectral theorem, in "
"which case $n$ is the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X},$ "
"$p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ are the eigenvalues of $\\rho,$ and "
"$\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ are orthonormal "
"eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang paraan para makakuha ng ganitong pagpapahayag ay sa pamamagitan ng "
"spectral theorem, kung saan ang $n$ ay ang bilang ng classical states ng "
"$\\mathsf{X},$ ang $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ ay ang mga eigenvalue ng $\\rho,$ "
"at ang $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ ay mga "
"orthonormal eigenvector na katumbas ng mga eigenvalue na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's actually no need to include the terms corresponding to the zero eigenvalues of $\\rho$ in the sum, which allows us to alternatively choose $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ and $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ to be the non-zero eigenvalues of $\\rho.$\n"
"This is the minimum value of $n$ for which an expression of $\\rho$ taking the form above exists.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi talaga kailangan isama sa sum ang mga term na katumbas ng zero eigenvalue ng $\\rho,$ na nagpapahintulot sa atin na pumili ng alternatibong $n = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho)$ at gawin ang $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ na mga hindi-zero na eigenvalue ng $\\rho.$\n"
"Ito ang pinakamaliit na halaga ng $n$ kung saan may pagpapahayag ng $\\rho$ na may ganitong anyo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, it is *not necessary* that the chosen expression of $\\rho,$ as a convex combination of pure states, comes from the spectral theorem — this is just one way to obtain such an expression.\n"
"In particular, $n$ could be any positive integer, the unit vectors $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal, and the probabilities $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ need not be eigenvalues of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para maging malinaw, *hindi kinakailangan* na ang napiling pagpapahayag ng $\\rho$ bilang convex combination ng pure states ay nagmula sa spectral theorem — ito ay isa lamang sa mga paraan para makakuha ng ganitong pagpapahayag.\n"
"Sa partikular, ang $n$ ay maaaring maging anumang positibong integer, ang mga unit vector na $\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\phi_{n-1}\\rangle$ ay hindi kailangang maging orthogonal, at ang mga probabilidad na $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ ay hindi kailangang maging eigenvalue ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can now identify a purification of $\\rho$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating tukuyin ang isang purification ng $\\rho$ tulad ng "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're making the assumption that the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ include $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"If they do not, an arbitrary choice for $n$ distinct classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ can be substituted for $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Verifying that this is indeed a purification of $\\rho$ is a simple matter of computing the partial trace, which can be done in the following two equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ipinapalagay natin na ang mga classical states ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay kinabibilangan ng $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Kung hindi, maaaring gamitin ang anumang pagpili ng $n$ na natatanging classical states ng $\\mathsf{Y}$ bilang kapalit ng $0,\\ldots,n-1.$\n"
"Ang pag-verify na ito ay talagang purification ng $\\rho$ ay simpleng bagay lamang ng pagkalkula ng partial trace, na maaaring gawin sa dalawang katumbas na paraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\langle a\\vert) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\\bigr) =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_b\\vert\n"
"\\, \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert a \\rangle \\langle b \\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle \\phi_a\\vert = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"More generally, for any orthonormal set of vectors "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\},$ the "
"quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mas pangkalahatang kalagayan, para sa anumang orthonormal na set ng mga "
"vector na "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{n-1}\\rangle\\},$ ang "
"quantum state vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert\\phi_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr "ay isang purification ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example {#example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa {#example}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits and\n"
msgstr "Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay parehong qubit at\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{3}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is a density matrix representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr "ay isang density matrix na kumakatawan sa estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can use the spectral theorem to express $\\rho$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating gamitin ang spectral theorem para ipahayag ang $\\rho$ "
"bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\cos^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert +\n"
"\\sin^2(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle\\langle\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"The quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle = \\cos(\\theta) \\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta)\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
"Ang quantum state vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\sin(\\pi/8) \\vert \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which describes a pure state of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ is "
"therefore a purification of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"na naglalarawan ng pure state ng pares na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}),$ ay "
"samakatuwid isang purification ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alternatively, we can write\n"
msgstr "Bilang alternatibo, maaari nating isulat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a convex combination of pure states but not a spectral decomposition because $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert +\\rangle$ are not orthogonal and $1/2$ is not an eigenvalue of $\\rho.$\n"
"Nevertheless, the quantum state vector\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay isang convex combination ng mga pure states ngunit hindi isang spectral decomposition dahil ang $\\vert 0\\rangle$ at $\\vert +\\rangle$ ay hindi orthogonal at ang $1/2$ ay hindi eigenvalue ng $\\rho.$\n"
"Gayunpaman, ang quantum state vector\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert + \\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Schmidt decompositions {#schmidt-decompositions}"
msgstr "Mga Schmidt decomposition {#schmidt-decompositions}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we will discuss *Schmidt decompositions*, which are expressions of quantum state vectors of *pairs* of systems that take a certain form.\n"
"Schmidt decompositions are closely connected with purifications, and they're very useful in their own right.\n"
"Indeed, when reasoning about a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems, the first step is often to identify or consider a Schmidt decomposition of this state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tatalakayin natin ang mga *Schmidt decomposition*, na mga pagpapahayag ng quantum state vector ng mga *pares* ng sistema na may tiyak na anyo.\n"
"Ang mga Schmidt decomposition ay malapit na konektado sa mga purification, at napaka-kapaki-pakinabang nila sa kanilang sarili.\n"
"Sa katunayan, kapag nag-iisip tungkol sa isang ibinigay na quantum state vector na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ng isang pares ng mga sistema, ang unang hakbang ay madalas na ang paghanap o pagsasaalang-alang ng isang Schmidt decomposition ng estado na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Definition\">\n"
"Let $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ be a given quantum state vector of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$ A *Schmidt decomposition* of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ is an expression of the form\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"where $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ are positive real numbers summing to $1$ and *both* of the sets $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Kahulugan\">\n"
"Hayaan ang $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ na maging isang ibinigay na quantum state vector ng pares ng mga sistema $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$ Ang *Schmidt decomposition* ng $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay isang pagpapahayag ng anyo\n"
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ ay mga positibong tunay na bilang na may kabuuan na $1$ at *parehong* mga set na $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ at $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay orthonormal.\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The values\n"
msgstr "Ang mga halaga\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{p_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{p_{r-1}}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ are known as its *Schmidt coefficients*, which are uniquely determined (up to their ordering) — they're the only positive real numbers that can appear in such an expression of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"The sets\n"
msgstr ""
"sa isang Schmidt decomposition ng $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay kilala bilang mga *Schmidt coefficient* nito, na natatanging natutukoy (hanggang sa kanilang pagkakasunud-sunod) — sila lamang ang mga positibong tunay na bilang na maaaring lumabas sa ganitong pagpapahayag ng $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Ang mga set\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\} \\quad\\text{at}\\quad\n"
"\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"on the other hand, are not uniquely determined, and the freedom one has in "
"choosing these sets of vectors will be clarified in the explanation that "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"sa kabilang banda, ay hindi natatanging natutukoy, at ang kalayaan sa "
"pagpili ng mga set ng mga vector na ito ay ipaliliwanag sa paliwanag na "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll now verify that a given quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ "
"does indeed have a Schmidt decomposition, and in the process, we'll learn "
"how to find one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susuriin natin ngayon na ang isang ibinigay na quantum state vector na "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ay mayroon talagang Schmidt decomposition, at sa "
"proseso, matututo tayo kung paano ito hanapin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider first an arbitrary (not necessarily orthogonal) basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to the system $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Because this is a basis, there will always exist a uniquely determined selection of vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the following equation is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang muna ang isang arbitrary (hindi kinakailangang orthogonal) na basis na $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ng vector space na katumbas ng sistema $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Dahil ito ay isang basis, palaging mayroon talagang natatanging napiling mga vector na $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ kung saan totoo ang sumusunod na equation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a \\rangle\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, suppose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is the standard basis associated with $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Assuming the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ this means that $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ and we find that\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, ipagpalagay na ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay ang standard basis na katumbas ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Assuming na ang classical state set ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay $\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ ibig sabihin nito na $\\vert x_a\\rangle = \\vert a\\rangle$ para sa bawat $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ at mahahanap natin na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "when\n"
msgstr "kapag\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = ( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}.$\n"
"We frequently consider expressions like this when contemplating a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa bawat $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\}.$\n"
"Madalas nating isaalang-alang ang mga ganitong pagpapahayag kapag pinag-iisipan ang isang standard basis measurement ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "It's important to note that the formula\n"
msgstr "Mahalagang tandaan na ang formula\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ in this example only works because $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* basis.\n"
"In general, if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis that is not necessarily orthonormal, then the vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ are still uniquely determined by the equation $(1),$ but a different formula is needed.\n"
"One way to find them is first to identify vectors $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ so that the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa mga vector na $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ sa halimbawang ito ay gumagana lamang dahil ang $\\{\\vert 0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert n-1\\rangle\\}$ ay isang *orthonormal* na basis.\n"
"Sa pangkalahatan, kung ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay isang basis na hindi kinakailangang orthonormal, kung gayon ang mga vector na $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ ay natatanging natutukoy pa rin ng equation na $(1),$ ngunit kailangan ng ibang formula.\n"
"Isang paraan para mahanap ang mga ito ay ang unang tukuyin ang mga vector na $\\vert w_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert w_{n-1}\\rangle$ upang masiyahan ang equation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle w_a \\vert x_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases} 1 & a=b\\\\ 0 & a\\neq b \\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied for all $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ at which point we have\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa lahat ng $a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\},$ at sa puntong iyon ay mayroon"
" tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert z_a \\rangle = (\\langle w_a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}) \\vert \\psi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a given basis $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ of the vector space corresponding to $\\mathsf{X},$ the uniquely determined vectors $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ for which the equation $(1)$ is satisfied won't necessarily satisfy any special properties, even if $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ happens to be an orthonormal basis.\n"
"If, however, we choose $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be an orthonormal basis of *eigenvectors* of the reduced state\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang ibinigay na basis na $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ng vector space na katumbas ng $\\mathsf{X},$ ang natatanging natutukoy na mga vector na $\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle$ kung saan nasiyahan ang equation na $(1)$ ay hindi kinakailangang matugunan ang anumang espesyal na katangian, kahit na ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay orthonormal na basis.\n"
"Gayunpaman, kung pipiliin natin ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ bilang isang orthonormal na basis ng mga *eigenvector* ng reduced state\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\bigl( \\vert \\psi\\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert \\bigr),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"then something interesting happens.\n"
"Specifically, for the uniquely determined collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true, we find that this collection must be *orthogonal.*\n"
msgstr ""
"may mangyayaring kawili-wili.\n"
"Sa partikular, para sa natatanging napiling koleksyon na $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ kung saan totoo ang equation na $(1),$ mahahanap natin na ang koleksyong ito ay kailangang maging *orthogonal.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "In greater detail, consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mas detalyadong paliwanag, isaalang-alang ang isang spectral "
"decomposition ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we're denoting the eigenvalues of $\\rho$ by $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ in recognition of the fact that $\\rho$ is a density matrix — so the vector of eigenvalues $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ forms a probability vector — while $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors corresponding to these eigenvalues.\n"
"To see that the unique collection $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ for which the equation $(1)$ is true is necessarily orthogonal, we can begin by computing the partial trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito tinutukoy natin ang mga eigenvalue ng $\\rho$ bilang $p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1}$ bilang pagkilala sa katotohanang ang $\\rho$ ay isang density matrix — kaya ang vector ng mga eigenvalue na $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{n-1})$ ay bumubuo ng isang probability vector — habang ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay isang orthonormal na basis ng mga eigenvector na katumbas ng mga eigenvalue na ito.\n"
"Upang makita na ang natatanging koleksyon na $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ kung saan totoo ang equation na $(1)$ ay kailangang maging orthogonal, maaari tayong magsimula sa pag-compute ng partial trace.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert z_a\\rangle\\langle z_b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\langle z_b\\vert z_a\\rangle \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This expression must agree with the spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
"Because $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is a basis, we conclude that the set of matrices\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pagpapahayag na ito ay dapat na sumasang-ayon sa spectral decomposition ng $\\rho.$\n"
"Dahil ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay isang basis, mayroon tayong konklusyon na ang set ng mga matrix\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\{ \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_b\\vert \\,:\\, a,b\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n-1\\} \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is linearly independent, and so it follows that\n"
msgstr "ay linearly independent, at kaya sumusunod na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle z_b \\vert z_a\\rangle =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"  p_a & a=b\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  0 & a\\neq b,\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"establishing that $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ "
"is orthogonal.\n"
msgstr ""
"na nagpapatunay na ang $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"z_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay orthogonal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've nearly obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"It remains to discard those terms in $(1)$ for which $p_a = 0$ and then write $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for a unit vector $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each of the remaining terms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halos nakuha na natin ang isang Schmidt decomposition ng $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Natitira na lang ang pagtatapon ng mga term sa $(1)$ kung saan $p_a = 0$ at pagkatapos ay isulat ang $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para sa isang unit vector na $\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para sa bawat isa sa mga natitirang term.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A convenient way to do this begins with the observation that we're free to "
"number the eigenvalue/eigenvector pairs in a spectral decomposition of the "
"reduced state $\\rho$ however we wish — so we may assume that the "
"eigenvalues are sorted in decreasing order:\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang maginhawang paraan para gawin ito ay nagsisimula sa obserbasyon na "
"malaya tayong bilangin ang mga eigenvalue/eigenvector na pares sa isang "
"spectral decomposition ng reduced state na $\\rho$ sa anumang paraan na "
"gusto natin — kaya maaari tayong ipagpalagay na ang mga eigenvalue ay "
"nakaayos sa bumababang pagkakasunud-sunod:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p_0 \\geq p_1 \\geq \\cdots \\geq p_{n-1}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Letting $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho),$ we find that $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ and $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0.$\n"
"So, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Habang tinutukoy ang $r = \\operatorname{rank}(\\rho),$ mahahanap natin na $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1} > 0$ at $p_r = \\cdots = p_{n-1} = 0.$\n"
"Kaya, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} p_a \\vert x_a \\rangle \\langle x_a \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and we can write the quantum state vector $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"at maisusulat natin ang quantum state vector na $\\vert \\psi \\rangle$ "
"bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert z_a\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Given that\n"
msgstr "Dahil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\| \\vert z_a \\rangle \\|^2 = \\langle z_a \\vert z_a \\rangle = p_a > 0\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $a=0,\\ldots,r-1,$ we can define unit vectors $\\vert y_0 "
"\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ as\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa $a=0,\\ldots,r-1,$ maaari nating tukuyin ang mga unit vector na "
"$\\vert y_0 \\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle$ bilang\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert y_a\\rangle = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\|\\vert z_a\\rangle\\|} = \\frac{\\vert z_a\\rangle}{\\sqrt{p_a}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so that $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}.$\n"
"Because the vectors $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthogonal and nonzero, it follows that\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an *orthonormal* set, and so we have obtained a Schmidt decomposition of $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"upang ang $\\vert z_a\\rangle = \\sqrt{p_a}\\vert y_a\\rangle$ para sa bawat $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,r-1\\}.$\n"
"Dahil ang mga vector na $\\{\\vert z_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert z_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay orthogonal at hindi-zero, sumusunod na\n"
"ang $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle, \\ldots, \\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay isang *orthonormal* na set, at kaya nakuha na natin ang isang Schmidt decomposition ng $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert y_a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Concerning the choice of the vectors\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},$\n"
"we can select $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (as we have done above), in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tungkol sa pagpili ng mga vector\n"
"$\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ at\n"
"$\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\},$\n"
"maaari nating piliin ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ bilang anumang orthonormal na set ng mga eigenvector na katumbas ng mga hindi-zero na eigenvalue ng reduced state na $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ (tulad ng nagawa natin sa itaas), at sa kasong iyon ang mga vector na $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay natatanging natutukoy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The situation is symmetric between the two systems, so we can alternatively "
"choose $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ to be any "
"orthonormal set of eigenvectors corresponding to the nonzero eigenvalues of "
"the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert),$ "
"in which case the vectors $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ will be uniquely determined.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sitwasyon ay simetrikal sa pagitan ng dalawang sistema, kaya maaari rin "
"tayong pumili ng $\\{\\vert y_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert y_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ "
"bilang anumang orthonormal na set ng mga eigenvector na katumbas ng mga "
"hindi-zero na eigenvalue ng reduced state na "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert),$ "
"at sa kasong iyon ang mga vector na $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert "
"x_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay matutukoy.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice, however, that once one of the sets is selected, as a set of "
"eigenvectors of the corresponding reduced state as just described, the other"
" is determined — so they cannot be chosen independently.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin, gayunpaman, na kapag napili na ang isa sa mga set bilang set ng "
"mga eigenvector ng katumbas na reduced state tulad ng inilarawan, ang isa pa"
" ay natutukoy na — kaya hindi sila maaaring piliin nang nagsasarili.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although it won't come up again in this series, it is noteworthy that the "
"non-zero eigenvalues $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ of the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"must always agree with the nonzero eigenvalues of the reduced state "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"for any pure state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ of a pair of systems "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kahit hindi na ito darating muli sa seryeng ito, kapansin-pansin na ang mga "
"hindi-zero na eigenvalue na $p_0,\\ldots,p_{r-1}$ ng reduced state na "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"ay palaging dapat na sumasang-ayon sa mga hindi-zero na eigenvalue ng "
"reduced state na "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert)$ "
"para sa anumang pure state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ ng pares ng mga sistema "
"$(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, the reduced states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ have exactly the same amount of randomness in them when the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in a pure state.\n"
"This fact is revealed by the Schmidt decomposition: in both cases the eigenvalues of the reduced states must agree with the squares of the Schmidt coefficients of the pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa intuitive na pagsasalita, ang mga reduced state ng $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay may eksaktong parehong halaga ng randomness sa kanila kapag ang pares na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ ay nasa isang pure state.\n"
"Inihahayag ng Schmidt decomposition ang katotohanang ito: sa parehong kaso ang mga eigenvalue ng mga reduced state ay dapat na sumasang-ayon sa mga parisukat ng mga Schmidt coefficient ng pure state.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unitary equivalence of purifications {#unitary-equivalence-of-purifications}"
msgstr ""
"Unitary equivalence ng mga purification {#unitary-equivalence-of-"
"purifications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can use Schmidt decompositions to establish a fundamentally important "
"fact concerning purifications known as the *unitary equivalence of "
"purifications*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating gamitin ang mga Schmidt decomposition para maitatag ang isang "
"mahalagang katotohanang tungkol sa mga purification na kilala bilang "
"*unitary equivalence ng mga purification*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Unitary equivalence of purifications: Suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are systems, and $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that both purify the same state of $\\mathsf{X}.$ In symbols,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"There must then exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ alone that transforms the first purification into the second:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorema\">\n"
"Unitary equivalence ng mga purification: Ipagpalagay na ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay mga sistema, at ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ at $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ ay mga quantum state vector ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ na parehong nagpu-purify ng parehong estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$ Sa simbolo,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
"para sa ilang density matrix na $\\rho$ na kumakatawan sa estado ng $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Dapat na mayroon talagang unitary operation na $U$ sa $\\mathsf{Y}$ lamang na nagko-convert ng unang purification sa pangalawa:\n"
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\phi\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll discuss a few implications of this theorem as the lesson continues, "
"but first let's see how it follows from our previous discussion of Schmidt "
"decompositions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tatalakayin natin ang ilang implikasyon ng teoremang ito habang nagpapatuloy"
" ang aralin, ngunit una, tingnan natin kung paano ito sumusunod mula sa "
"ating nakaraang talakayan ng mga Schmidt decomposition.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our assumption is that $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ are quantum state vectors\n"
"of a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ that satisfy the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ating pagpapalagay ay ang $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ at $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ ay mga quantum state vector\n"
"ng pares ng mga sistema $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ na nasiyahan ang equation\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert) = \\rho =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa ilang density matrix na $\\rho$ na kumakatawan sa estado ng "
"$\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Consider a spectral decomposition of $\\rho.$\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang isang spectral decomposition ng $\\rho.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{n-1} p_a \\vert x_a\\rangle\\langle x_a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ is an orthonormal basis of eigenvectors of $\\rho.$\n"
"By following the prescription described previously we can obtain Schmidt decompositions for both $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ having the following form.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dito ang $\\{\\vert x_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert x_{n-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay isang orthonormal na basis ng mga eigenvector ng $\\rho.$\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagsunod sa pamamaraang inilarawan kanina, makakakuha tayo ng mga Schmidt decomposition para sa parehong $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ at $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ na may sumusunod na anyo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\phi\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these expressions $r$ is the rank of $\\rho$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ are orthonormal sets of vectors in the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa mga pagpapahayag na ito, ang $r$ ay ang rank ng $\\rho$ at\n"
"ang $\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ at\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{r-1}\\rangle\\}$ ay mga orthonormal na set ng mga vector sa espasyo na katumbas ng $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For any two orthonormal sets in the same space that have the same number of elements, there's always a unitary matrix that transforms the first set into the second, so we can choose a unitary matrix $U$ so that $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ for $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1.$\n"
"In particular, to find such a matrix $U$ we can first use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to extend our orthonormal sets to orthonormal bases\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ and\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\},$ where $m$ is the dimension of the space corresponding to $\\mathsf{Y},$ and then take\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa anumang dalawang orthonormal na set sa parehong espasyo na may parehong bilang ng mga elemento, palaging may unitary matrix na nagko-convert ng unang set sa pangalawa, kaya maaari tayong pumili ng unitary matrix na $U$ upang ang $U \\vert u_a\\rangle = \\vert v_a\\rangle$ para sa $a = 0,\\ldots,r-1.$\n"
"Sa partikular, para mahanap ang ganitong matrix na $U,$ maaari nating gamitin muna ang Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process para palawakin ang ating mga orthonormal na set sa mga orthonormal na basis\n"
"$\\{\\vert u_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert u_{m-1}\\rangle\\}$ at\n"
"$\\{\\vert v_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert v_{m-1}\\rangle\\},$ kung saan ang $m$ ay ang dimensyon ng espasyo na katumbas ng $\\mathsf{Y},$ at pagkatapos ay kumuha ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert v_a\\rangle\\langle u_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We now find that\n"
msgstr "Mahahanap natin ngayon na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes U \\vert u_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{r-1} \\sqrt{p_a} \\, \\vert x_a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert v_a\\rangle\\\\\n"
"& = \\vert\\phi\\rangle,\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which completes the proof.\n"
msgstr "na nagkukumpleto ng patunay.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are just a few of many interesting examples and implications connected with the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"We'll see another critically important one later in the lesson, in the context of fidelity, known as *Uhlmann's theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang ilang sa maraming kawili-wiling halimbawa at implikasyon na konektado sa unitary equivalence ng mga purification.\n"
"Makikita natin ang isa pang kritikal na mahalaga sa ibang pagkakataon sa aralin, sa konteksto ng fidelity, na kilala bilang *Uhlmann's theorem*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"
msgstr "Superdense coding {#superdense-coding}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the superdense coding protocol, Alice and Bob share an e-bit, meaning that Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A},$ Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ and together the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is in the $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$ Bell state.\n"
"The protocol describes how Alice can transform this shared state into any one of the four Bell states, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle,$ and\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle,$ by applying a unitary operation to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"Once she has done this, she sends $\\mathsf{A}$ to Bob, and then Bob performs a measurement on the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ to see which Bell state he holds.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa superdense coding protocol, nagbabahagi sina Alice at Bob ng isang e-bit, ibig sabihin ang Alice ay may hawak na isang qubit na $\\mathsf{A},$ si Bob ay may hawak na isang qubit na $\\mathsf{B},$ at ang pares na $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ ay nasa $\\vert\\phi^{+}\\rangle$ Bell state.\n"
"Inilalarawan ng protocol kung paano maaaring baguhin ni Alice ang shared state na ito sa alinman sa apat na Bell state, $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle,$ $\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle,$ at\n"
"$\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle,$ sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng isang unitary operation sa kanyang qubit na $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
"Kapag nagawa na niya ito, ipinapadala niya ang $\\mathsf{A}$ kay Bob, at pagkatapos ay nagsasagawa si Bob ng measurement sa pares na $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ upang malaman kung aling Bell state ang hawak niya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For all four Bell states, the reduced state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B}$ is "
"the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa lahat ng apat na Bell state, ang reduced state ng qubit ni Bob na "
"$\\mathsf{B}$ ay ang completely mixed state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle\\langle\\phi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\phi^-\\rangle\\langle\\phi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^+\\rangle\\langle\\psi^+\\vert) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi^-\\rangle\\langle\\psi^-\\vert) =\n"
"\\frac{\\mathbb{I}}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the unitary equivalence of purifications, we immediately conclude that for each Bell state there must exist a unitary operation on Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ alone that transforms $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ into the chosen Bell state.\n"
"Although this does not reveal the precise details of the protocol, the unitary equivalence of purifications does immediately imply that superdense coding is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng unitary equivalence ng mga purification, agad nating masasabi na para sa bawat Bell state ay dapat na mayroon talagang unitary operation sa qubit ni Alice na $\\mathsf{A}$ lamang na nagko-convert ng $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ sa piniling Bell state.\n"
"Kahit hindi nito inihahayag ang eksaktong detalye ng protocol, ang unitary equivalence ng mga purification ay agad na nagpapahiwatig na posible ang superdense coding.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also conclude that generalizations of superdense coding to larger "
"systems are always possible, provided that we replace the Bell states with "
"any orthonormal basis of purifications of the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari rin tayong magtapos na ang mga generalization ng superdense coding sa"
" mas malalaking sistema ay palaging posible, basta't pinalitan natin ang mga"
" Bell state ng anumang orthonormal na basis ng mga purification ng "
"completely mixed state.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Cryptographic implications {#cryptographic-implications}"
msgstr "Mga implikasyon sa cryptography {#cryptographic-implications}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unitary equivalence of purifications has implications concerning the implementation of cryptographic primitives using quantum information.\n"
"For instance, the unitary equivalence of purifications reveals that it is impossible to implement an ideal form of *bit commitment* using quantum information.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unitary equivalence ng mga purification ay may mga implikasyon tungkol sa pagpapatupad ng mga cryptographic primitive gamit ang quantum information.\n"
"Halimbawa, inihahayag ng unitary equivalence ng mga purification na imposible ang pagpapatupad ng isang ideal na anyo ng *bit commitment* gamit ang quantum information.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bit commitment primitive involves two participants, Alice and Bob (who don't trust one another), and has two phases.\n"
"- The first phase is the *commit* phase, through which Alice commits to a binary value $b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"This commitment must be *binding*, which means that Alice cannot change her mind, as well as *concealing*, which means that Bob can't tell which value Alice has committed to.\n"
"- The second phase is the *reveal* phase, in which the bit committed by Alice becomes known to Bob, who should then be convinced that it was truly the committed value that was revealed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bit commitment primitive ay kinabibilangan ng dalawang kalahok, sina Alice at Bob (na hindi nagtitiwala sa isa't isa), at may dalawang phase.\n"
"- Ang unang phase ay ang *commit* phase, kung saan nag-co-commit si Alice sa isang binary na halaga na $b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Ang commitment na ito ay dapat na *binding*, ibig sabihin hindi maaaring magbago ng isip si Alice, pati na rin *concealing*, ibig sabihin hindi malalaman ni Bob kung aling halaga ang kinonmit ni Alice.\n"
"- Ang pangalawang phase ay ang *reveal* phase, kung saan ang bit na kinonmit ni Alice ay nalalaman ni Bob, na dapat ay makumbinsi na ang kinonmit na halaga talaga ang inihayag.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In intuitive, operational terms, the first phase of bit commitment should function as if Alice writes a binary value on a piece of paper, locks the paper inside of a safe, and gives the safe to Bob while keeping the key for herself.\n"
"Alice has committed to the binary value written on the paper because the safe is in Bob's possession (so it's binding), but because Bob can't open the safe he can't tell which value Alice committed to (so it's concealing).\n"
"The second phase should work as if Alice hands the key to the safe to Bob, so that he can open the safe to reveal the value to which Alice committed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa intuitive at operational na mga termino, ang unang phase ng bit commitment ay dapat gumana na parang si Alice ay sumulat ng binary na halaga sa isang piraso ng papel, kinulong ang papel sa loob ng isang kaha de yero (safe), at ibinigay ang safe kay Bob habang pinanatili niya ang susi para sa kanyang sarili.\n"
"Nag-commit si Alice sa binary na halagang nakasulat sa papel dahil ang safe ay nasa pag-aari ni Bob (kaya ito ay binding), ngunit dahil hindi mabuksan ni Bob ang safe ay hindi niya malalaman kung aling halaga ang kinonmit ni Alice (kaya ito ay concealing).\n"
"Ang pangalawang phase ay dapat gumana na parang ibinibigay ni Alice ang susi ng safe kay Bob, upang mabuksan niya ito para malaman ang halagang kinonmit ni Alice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As it turns out, it is impossible to implement a perfect bit commitment protocol by means of quantum information alone, for this contradicts the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
"Here is a high-level summary of an argument that establishes this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung tutuusin, imposible ang pagpapatupad ng isang perpektong bit commitment protocol sa pamamagitan ng quantum information lamang, dahil ito ay sumasalungat sa unitary equivalence ng mga purification.\n"
"Narito ang mataas na antas na buod ng isang argumento na nagpapatunay nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To begin, we can assume Alice and Bob only perform unitary operations or introduce new initialized systems as the protocol is executed.\n"
"The fact that every channel has a Stinespring representation allows us to make this assumption.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para magsimula, maaari nating ipagpalagay na sina Alice at Bob ay nagsasagawa lamang ng mga unitary operation o nagpapakilala ng mga bagong initialized na sistema habang isinasagawa ang protocol.\n"
"Ang katotohanan na ang bawat channel ay may Stinespring representation ay nagpapahintulot sa ating gumawa ng pagpapalagay na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of the commit phase of the protocol, Bob holds in his possession some compound system that must be in one of two quantum states: $\\rho_0$ if Alice committed to the value $0$ and $\\rho_1$ if Alice committed to the value $1.$\n"
"In order for the protocol to be perfectly concealing, Bob should not be able to tell the difference between these two states — so it must be that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1.$\n"
"(Otherwise there would be a measurement that discriminates these states probabilistically.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa katapusan ng commit phase ng protocol, si Bob ay may hawak sa kanyang pag-aari ng ilang compound system na dapat nasa isa sa dalawang quantum state: $\\rho_0$ kung ang Alice ay nag-commit sa halagang $0$ at $\\rho_1$ kung ang Alice ay nag-commit sa halagang $1.$\n"
"Para maging perpektong concealing ang protocol, si Bob ay hindi dapat makilala ang pagkakaiba sa pagitan ng dalawang estado na ito — kaya dapat na $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1.$\n"
"(Kung hindi, magkakaroon ng measurement na may kakayahang i-discriminate ang mga estado na ito nang probabilistiko.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, because Alice and Bob have only used unitary operations, the state of all of the systems involved in the protocol together after the commit phase must be in a pure state.\n"
"In particular, suppose that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $0,$ and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ is the pure state of all of the systems involved in the protocol when Alice commits to $1.$\n"
"If we write $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ to denote Alice and Bob's (possibly compound) systems, then\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, dahil ginamit lamang nina Alice at Bob ang mga unitary operation, ang estado ng lahat ng sistema na kasangkot sa protocol sa kabuuan pagkatapos ng commit phase ay dapat nasa isang pure state.\n"
"Sa partikular, ipagpalagay na ang $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ ay ang pure state ng lahat ng sistema na kasangkot sa protocol kapag nag-commit si Alice sa $0,$ at ang $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ ay ang pure state ng lahat ng sistema na kasangkot sa protocol kapag nag-commit si Alice sa $1.$\n"
"Kung isinulat natin ang $\\mathsf{A}$ at $\\mathsf{B}$ para tukuyin ang mga (posibleng compound) sistema nina Alice at Bob, kung gayon\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_0 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle\\langle\\psi_0\\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\rho_1 & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle\\langle\\psi_1\\vert).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given the requirement that $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ for a perfectly concealing "
"protocol, we find that $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ "
"are purifications of the same state — and so, by the unitary equivalence of "
"purifications, there must exist a unitary operation $U$ on $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"alone such that\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil sa kinakailangan na $\\rho_0 = \\rho_1$ para sa isang perpektong "
"concealing na protocol, mahahanap natin na ang $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle$ at "
"$\\vert\\psi_1\\rangle$ ay mga purification ng parehong estado — at kaya, sa"
" pamamagitan ng unitary equivalence ng mga purification, dapat na mayroon "
"talagang unitary operation na $U$ sa $\\mathsf{A}$ lamang tulad na\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(U\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}})\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle = \\vert\\psi_1\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice is therefore free to change her commitment from $0$ to $1$ by applying $U$ to $\\mathsf{A},$\n"
"or from $1$ to $0$ by applying $U^{\\dagger},$ and so the hypothetical protocol being considered completely fails to be binding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Samakatuwid, malaya si Alice na baguhin ang kanyang commitment mula $0$ patungong $1$ sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng $U$ sa $\\mathsf{A},$\n"
"o mula $1$ patungong $0$ sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng $U^{\\dagger},$ at kaya ang hypothetical na protocol na pinag-uusapan ay ganap na nabigo sa pagiging binding.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"
msgstr "Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem {#hughston-jozsa-wootters-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last implication of the unitary equivalence of purifications that we'll discuss in this portion of the lesson is the following theorem known as the Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem.\n"
"(This is, in fact, a slightly simplified statement of the theorem known by this name.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling implikasyon ng unitary equivalence ng mga purification na tatalakayin natin sa bahaging ito ng aralin ay ang sumusunod na teorema na kilala bilang Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters theorem.\n"
"(Ito ay, sa katunayan, isang bahagyang pinasimpleng pahayag ng teoremang kilala sa pangalang ito.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Theorem\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Let $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ be systems and let $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ be a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Also let $N$ be an arbitrary positive integer, let $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ be a probability vector, and let $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ be quantum state vectors representing states of $\\mathsf{X}$ such that\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"There exists a (general) measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$ such that the following two statements are true when this measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}$ when $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is in the state $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Teorema\">\n"
"Hughston-Jozsa-Wootters: Hayaan ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ na maging mga sistema at hayaan ang $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ na maging quantum state vector ng pares na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
"Hayaan din ang $N$ na maging isang arbitrary na positibong integer, hayaan ang $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{N-1})$ na maging isang probability vector, at hayaan ang $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ na maging mga quantum state vector na kumakatawan sa mga estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ tulad na\n"
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert\\bigr) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
"May (pangkalahatan) na measurement na $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ sa $\\mathsf{Y}$ tulad na ang sumusunod na dalawang pahayag ay totoo kapag isiniagawa ang measurement na ito sa $\\mathsf{Y}$ kapag ang $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ ay nasa estado na $\\vert\\phi\\rangle:$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ appears with probability"
" $p_a$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bawat measurement outcome na $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}$ ay lumalabas na "
"may probabilidad na $p_a$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"2. Conditioned on obtaining the measurement outcome $a,$ the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"2. Nakatakda sa pagkakuha ng measurement outcome na $a,$ ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagiging $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this theorem says that as long as we have a pure state of two systems, then for *any* way of thinking about the reduced state of the first system as a convex combination of pure states, there is a measurement of the second system that effectively makes this way of thinking about the first system a reality.\n"
"Notice that the number $N$ is not necessarily bounded by the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ or $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"For instance, it could be that $N = 1,000,000$ while $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa intuitive na pagsasalita, sinasabi ng teoremang ito na hangga't mayroon tayong pure state ng dalawang sistema, kung gayon para sa *anumang* paraan ng pag-iisip tungkol sa reduced state ng unang sistema bilang convex combination ng mga pure states, may measurement ng pangalawang sistema na epektibong ginagawang realidad ang paraan ng pag-iisip na ito tungkol sa unang sistema.\n"
"Pansinin na ang bilang na $N$ ay hindi kinakailangang nakatali sa bilang ng mga classical states ng $\\mathsf{X}$ o $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Halimbawa, maaaring $N = 1{,}000{,}000$ habang ang $\\mathsf{X}$ at $\\mathsf{Y}$ ay mga qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We shall prove this theorem using the unitary equivalence of purifications, beginning with the introduction of a new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Consider the following two quantum state vectors of the triple $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Patutunayin natin ang teoremang ito gamit ang unitary equivalence ng mga purification, simula sa pagpapakilala ng bagong sistema na $\\mathsf{Z}$ na ang classical state set ay $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Isaalang-alang ang sumusunod na dalawang quantum state vector ng triple na $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle & = \\vert\\phi\\rangle_{\\mathsf{XY}}\\otimes\\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle_{\\mathsf{Z}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first vector $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ is simply the given quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ tensored with $\\vert 0\\rangle$ for the new system $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
"For the second vector $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ we essentially have a quantum state vector that would make the theorem trivial — at least if $\\mathsf{Y}$ were replaced by $\\mathsf{Z}$ — because a standard basis measurement performed on $\\mathsf{Z}$ clearly yields each outcome $a$ with probability $p_a,$ and conditioned on obtaining this outcome the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ becomes $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang vector na $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ ay simpleng ang ibinigay na quantum state vector na $\\vert\\phi\\rangle$ na na-tensor sa $\\vert 0\\rangle$ para sa bagong sistema na $\\mathsf{Z}.$\n"
"Para sa pangalawang vector na $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ mayroon tayong essentially isang quantum state vector na gagawing trivial ang teorema — kahit papaano kung pinalitan ng $\\mathsf{Z}$ ang $\\mathsf{Y}$ — dahil ang isang standard basis measurement na isinasagawa sa $\\mathsf{Z}$ ay malinaw na nagbubunga ng bawat outcome na $a$ na may probabilidad na $p_a,$ at nakatakda sa pagkakuha ng outcome na ito, ang estado ng $\\mathsf{X}$ ay nagiging $\\vert\\psi_a\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By thinking about the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ as a single, compound"
" system that can be traced out to leave $\\mathsf{X},$ we find that we have "
"identified two different purifications of the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pamamagitan ng pag-iisip tungkol sa pares na $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ "
"bilang isang solong compound system na maaaring i-trace out para maiwan ang "
"$\\mathsf{X},$ mahahanap natin na natukoy na natin ang dalawang magkaibang "
"purification ng estado\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Specifically, for the first one we have\n"
msgstr "Sa partikular, para sa una ay mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_0\\vert)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (\\vert\\phi\\rangle\\langle\\phi\\vert) = \\rho\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and for the second one we have\n"
msgstr "at para sa pangalawa ay mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{YZ}} (\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\\langle\\gamma_1\\vert)\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{N-1} \\sqrt{p_a}\\sqrt{p_b} \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b\\vert)\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{N-1} p_a \\, \\vert\\psi_a\\rangle\\langle\\psi_a\\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\rho.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There must therefore exist a unitary operation $U$ on "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"Dapat na mayroon talagang unitary operation na $U$ sa "
"$(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ na nasiyahan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}} \\otimes U) \\vert \\gamma_0 \\rangle = \\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "by the unitary equivalence of purifications.\n"
msgstr "sa pamamagitan ng unitary equivalence ng mga purification.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using this unitary operation $U,$ we can implement a measurement that satisfies the requirements of the theorem as the following diagram illustrates.\n"
"In words, we introduce the new system $\\mathsf{Z}$ initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state, apply $U$ to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}),$ which transforms the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ from $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ into $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ and then measure $\\mathsf{Z}$ with a standard basis measurement, which we've already observed gives the desired behavior.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamit ang unitary operation na $U$ na ito, maaari tayong magpatupad ng measurement na nakakatugon sa mga kinakailangan ng teorema tulad ng inilalarawan ng sumusunod na diagram.\n"
"Sa mga salita, ipinakilala natin ang bagong sistema na $\\mathsf{Z}$ na na-initialize sa estado na $\\vert 0\\rangle,$ inilapat ang $U$ sa $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z}),$ na nagko-convert ng estado ng $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{Z})$ mula sa $\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle$ patungong $\\vert\\gamma_1\\rangle,$ at pagkatapos ay sinusukat ang $\\mathsf{Z}$ gamit ang isang standard basis measurement, na naobserbahan na nating nagbibigay ng nais na gawi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A quantum circuit implementation of a measurement for the HSW "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![A quantum circuit implementation of a measurement for the HSW "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/purifications-and-fidelity/HSW-measurement.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The dotted rectangle in the figure represents an implementation of this "
"measurement, which can be described as a collection of positive semidefinite"
" matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dotted na rektanggulo sa figure ay kumakatawan sa pagpapatupad ng "
"measurement na ito, na maaaring ilarawan bilang isang koleksyon ng mga "
"positive semidefinite matrix na $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{N-1}\\}$ tulad ng "
"sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert)U (\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
